{"id": "EUVD-2026-58977", "enisaUuid": "133b96c8-cdd3-317b-b503-ec504bc2e5bd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmacsec: don't read an unset MAC header in macsec_encrypt()\n\nmacsec_encrypt() reads the Ethernet header via eth_hdr(skb)\n(skb->head + skb->mac_header) to memmove() the 12 source/destination MAC\nbytes forward and make room for the SecTAG.\n\nOn the AF_PACKET SOCK_RAW + PACKET_QDISC_BYPASS transmit path the skb\nreaches the macsec ndo_start_xmit() with the MAC header unset, so\neth_hdr(skb) resolves to skb->head + (u16)~0 and the read is out of\nbounds: a 12-byte heap over-read that is also emitted on the wire as the\nframe's outer source/destination MAC. KASAN reports a slab-out-of-bounds\nread in macsec_start_xmit() on 6.0; on current mainline a CONFIG_DEBUG_NET\nbuild flags it as an unset mac header in skb_mac_header().\n\nOn the TX path the L2 header is at skb->data, so use skb_eth_hdr(), added\nby commit 96cc4b69581d (\"macvlan: do not assume mac_header is set in\nmacvlan_broadcast()\") for exactly this purpose.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:51:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:19:23", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6cec6187b8632423cd99a94fd5e5ba165fa2a33", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3adea1b1c04b57e08a5c12a1f42483760581ce61", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc9ffa1905e72f026d080880a2e4cfc42aa91000", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f21fa533a3ed15ada74106aac4b9ddd078fc6b7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e17a42199824973cd8212e95b21ffadf4114a21b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2cf10d042562283ff4ae97c02d0993d4f1b5ea29", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c39087ad0b97fc11a3b058dfc8db9fd370762cb9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5089008f90c0a7c5520dff3934e0af00adf322d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72019", "GHSA-593p-5684-69pq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "35647647-9a3d-3bfd-bbe3-cfa291d67d82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "35eac272-c72e-316b-b9af-1f16bd0151fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "6ff99475-bc55-3223-8a9c-e41fc3a105e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "767047e8-9f5b-3039-8232-fc34c78a6c36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c09440f7dcb304002dfced8c0fea289eb25f2da0 <dc9ffa1905e72f026d080880a2e4cfc42aa91000"}, {"id": "7da918c0-4644-32ba-95fa-a4b24ab8def5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c09440f7dcb304002dfced8c0fea289eb25f2da0 <2cf10d042562283ff4ae97c02d0993d4f1b5ea29"}, {"id": "7e839297-6594-3086-a8e2-7f8a6033e259", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "9f126b5d-ba24-37de-b560-142034650c02", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "b16ceb86-8a45-38d1-8c6f-c19f01e91980", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "b2307bc2-a607-3145-8d9c-06499357b659", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "b87062d3-424e-3355-aeb2-aa14b16bff1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c09440f7dcb304002dfced8c0fea289eb25f2da0 <c39087ad0b97fc11a3b058dfc8db9fd370762cb9"}, {"id": "baed47b8-ec92-390e-bc2a-c817db898f71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "d6581459-69b9-3311-a17e-8e3b706366eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c09440f7dcb304002dfced8c0fea289eb25f2da0 <e17a42199824973cd8212e95b21ffa